From c9e137c26cd4a5da19f27e0f85c92b9e0d4054bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lie Ryan <lie.ryan@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Mar 2025 06:29:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] alarmtimer: Fix argument order in alarm_timer_forward()

[ Upstream commit 5d16467ae56314d58f22b1f4580ec1ba30a48411 ]

The alarm_timer_forward() callback passes its arguments to
alarm_forward() in the wrong order, which results in the wrong
interval being used to forward the timer.

The consequence is missed expirations or incorrect overrun
accounting. Android uses alarmtimer frequently (every suspend-resume
cycle and every AlarmManager wakeup), so bad overrun accounting feeds
back into wrong suspend decisions — the wakeup-minimization logic in
this pipeline depends on correct expiry bookkeeping.

The Hipuu 6.6.142 fork already carries the fix; this patch targets the
stock OnePlusOSS 6.6.118 base and is skipped there via the marker
guard in action.yml (grep for the corrected argument order).

Fixes: 1c1e35611d8e ("alarmtimers: Rate limit starting alarmtimer on suspend")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Lie Ryan <lie.ryan@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Thomas Gleixner <tglx@linutronix.de>
---
 kernel/time/alarmtimer.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/kernel/time/alarmtimer.c b/kernel/time/alarmtimer.c
--- a/kernel/time/alarmtimer.c
+++ b/kernel/time/alarmtimer.c
@@ -611 +611 @@
-	return alarm_forward(alarm, timr->it_interval, now);
+	return alarm_forward(alarm, now, timr->it_interval);
